fieldSetT -- `x.name = v` WRITES THE FIELD x (SEQ 295 R3, branch groupFieldSetter).

One setter, setGroupField(target, number, value), holds every groupField write case.
`x :. name` calls it with 1; `x.name = v` reaches opAssign with opDot's COPY of the
field (marked isAccessorProduct, parented to x), and opAssign calls it with v.

Rows: FS-1 and FS-2 are a pair on a global (lastIndent) -- 7 then 0, read back each
time, so neither can pass on a default, and 7 proves the VALUE is carried, not just a
truth. The dispatch named processingCodE for this pair; it cannot be driven: once
processingCode is 1, aCTionXpress (ruleActions.rtn, `if !processingCode && method`)
stops running expressions -- the `= 0` that would undo it never runs, and neither does
the rest of the file. Measured: the write of 1 lands (reads 1), the write of 0 does not.
lastIndent is lastINDENT, the parser's indent; a top-level call sits at indent 0, so the
pair ends where it began, and the sentinel below is what says the parse survived it. FS-3 is `:.` unchanged. FS-4 clears the flag FS-3
set (1 -> 0), and FS-5/FS-6 are its non-zero sibling on a fresh field (0 -> 1). FS-7 is a
groupField with no write case (taG): opAssign says so by name on stderr and the tag stays.

Before the setter (H7): FS-1 read 0, FS-4 read 1, FS-6 read 0 -- `=` wrote only the copy.
